ed ObservedWriteScope. A transitive forced write invisible at plan-authoring time; 16 SKILL.md files sit under that pin. Resolved by authorized amendment rather than deferral, since deferring would leave a knowingly-red suite behind a close criterion demanding green. (3) F52: the spec glosses its file scope as bound by change.plan-scope-exceeds-spec, which compares DurableScope anchors at warning severity and never looks at file paths. Third check in this bundle found weaker than its description, with F49 and the validate:marketplace green that only proves the two trees agree (F46). (4) F48: the criterion enumerated its diagnostics by HEAD trigger, and the repair moved the mapping, so change.invalid-clarification-target would have kept its guide and emission site while losing test coverage; a fourth plant on a non-family child keeps it live. (5) F50: the plan's design note instructs expanding its own ObservedWriteScope, which the same plan's immutability forbids — inherited from the model plan for a second consecutive bundle, and fixed at the template source rather than here. Cursor companions are therefore disclosed-unlisted. (6) The spec and plan were amended in place while approved, under explicit authorization, twice: the src/lint narrowing that admitted the two exact guides, and the ObservedWriteScope amendment above.</Verdict></Verdicts></C-GRAMMAR-SEAM></NgraceRunLedger>
